# Contributor Covenant Code of Conduct

## Our Pledge

We as contributors and maintainers of the Simple Interest Calculator project pledge to make participation in this project a welcoming, respectful, and harassment-free experience for everyone, regardless of background, experience level, or identity.

We commit to treating all contributors, users, and community members with respect and professionalism.

## Our Standards

Examples of behavior that contribute to a positive environment include:

* Being respectful and considerate of others.
* Providing constructive feedback.
* Accepting different opinions and approaches.
* Focusing on what is best for the project and its users.
* Communicating clearly and professionally.
* Helping new contributors understand the project.

Unacceptable behavior includes:

* Harassment, discrimination, or personal attacks.
* Trolling or insulting comments.
* Publishing private or confidential information without permission.
* Unwelcome sexual attention or inappropriate behavior.
* Any other conduct that would reasonably be considered inappropriate in a professional or open-source community.

## Enforcement Responsibilities

Project maintainers are responsible for clarifying and enforcing the standards of acceptable behavior. They may take appropriate and fair corrective action in response to behavior that violates this Code of Conduct.

Maintainers may remove, edit, or reject contributions, comments, issues, or other interactions that violate these standards.

## Scope

This Code of Conduct applies within all project spaces, including the GitHub repository, issues, pull requests, discussions, and other project-related communication.

It also applies when an individual is officially representing the Simple Interest Calculator project in public spaces.

## Enforcement

Instances of unacceptable behavior may be reported to the project maintainers through the project's GitHub repository.

All reports will be reviewed fairly and, where appropriate, investigated. Maintainers will respect the privacy of people who report incidents and will handle reports as confidentially as reasonably possible.

## Enforcement Guidelines

Project maintainers may take one or more of the following actions depending on the circumstances:

1. A private or public warning.
2. Removal or editing of inappropriate comments or contributions.
3. Temporary restriction from participating in project discussions.
4. Temporary or permanent removal of contribution privileges.
5. Permanent removal from project spaces for serious or repeated violations.

The response will be proportionate to the nature and severity of the violation.

## Attribution

This Code of Conduct is inspired by the [Contributor Covenant](https://www.contributor-covenant.org/), a widely used standard for open-source communities.

The Simple Interest Calculator project may adapt these guidelines as necessary to meet the needs of its community.
